  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-29a60c84-7fff-e492-7889-2bbeada51608&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;On the balance of probability, the evidence does not demonstrate that the ground and first floor have been in continuous use as a single dwellinghouse for a minimum of four years. Prior to December 2024, the correct characterisation was a mixed residential and commercial use. The statutory requirements for a Certificate of Lawfulness are therefore not satisfied, and the application should be refused.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
